# Data licences

The MIT licence in `LICENSE` covers the source code of this repository. It does not cover the
data files listed here. Those files come from the Zebrafish Information Network (ZFIN) and from
the Zebrafish Anatomy Ontology (ZFA) and the Zebrafish Stage Ontology (ZFS). They keep their own
licences, and so do the fields of this repository that are derived from them.

`public/ATTRIBUTION.md` carries the same statements in the form the application shows them.

## ZFIN database files: CC BY 4.0

Files:

- `data/zfin/anatomy_item.txt`
- `data/zfin/anatomy_relationship.txt`
- `data/zfin/anatomy_synonyms.txt`
- `data/zfin/stage_ontology.txt`

Source: https://zfin.org/downloads, retrieved 2026-09-06. ZFIN data and data annotations are
licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International licence
(https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/), stated at
https://zfin.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/general/pages/1942160112.

Attribution: Zebrafish Information Network (ZFIN), University of Oregon, https://zfin.org. Cite
Bradford YM, Van Slyke CE, Ruzicka L, et al. Zebrafish information network, the knowledgebase for
Danio rerio research. Genetics 2022;220(4):iyac016.

The four files above are unchanged copies. The fields derived from them are also CC BY 4.0:

- the ZFA term ids, term names, synonyms and parent relations in `src/data/structures/*.json` and
  `src/data/vocabulary.json`
- the ZFS stage ids, stage names and hpf bounds in `src/data/stages.json`
- the start-stage and end-stage window of every record in `src/data/structures/*.json`
- the generated index `docs/SOURCES.md`, where it repeats those values

Modification: the ids, names and windows were copied into JSON records and re-keyed for the
application. No value was changed.

## ZFA and ZFS ontology file: CC BY 3.0

File: `data/zfin/zfa.obo`, OBO release 2026-07-16, retrieved 2026-09-06 from
http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/zfa.obo. The file header states the Creative Commons Attribution
3.0 licence (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/).

Attribution: the Zebrafish Anatomy Ontology (ZFA) and the Zebrafish Stage Ontology (ZFS), ZFIN.

`data/zfin/zfa.obo` is an unchanged copy. The term definitions taken from it are modified, on two
paths, and both modifications are stated here as CC BY asks:

- `src/data/vocabulary.json` keeps the first sentence of each definition and drops the rest. The
  HTML markup that sixteen ZFA definitions carry is removed first. A first sentence longer than
  240 characters is cut at the last sentence end that fits, or at a word gap with an ellipsis when
  it carries none.
- The definitions of the 221 records in `src/data/structures/*.json` are not cut to that length.
  Many of them run longer than 240 characters and carry more than one sentence. Some of them drop
  a trailing sentence of the ZFA text.

Most of the 221 record definitions are cuts of the ZFA text. Two are reworded.
ZFA:0000031 (hypochord) fixes a repeated phrase in the ZFA definition and drops a trailing
sentence. ZFA:0009288 (primordial germ cell) changes the ZFA definition from plural forms to
singular. The vocabulary definitions in `src/data/vocabulary.json` are cuts only. None of them are
reworded.

## Everything else

The geometry, the sizes, the positions, the colours, the events and the modelling notes in
`src/data/` are this project's own work and are covered by the MIT licence in `LICENSE`. ZFIN
supplies the vocabulary, not the geometry, and has reviewed none of it.

Stage times, embryo lengths and head-trunk angles read from the ZFIN staging series pages come
from Kimmel CB, Ballard WW, Kimmel SR, Ullmann B, Schilling TF (1995) Dev Dyn 203:253-310. ZFIN
reprints that article by a permission Wiley-Liss granted to ZFIN, and that permission is not part
of the ZFIN CC BY 4.0 grant. This repository takes numbers and landmark facts from those pages and
states them in its own words. It reproduces no sentence, table image or figure.

The licences of the bundled npm packages are in `public/THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt`.
